  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: 
    basic: GLP1-R is a transmembrane protein, meaning that it spans the entire thickness
      of the cell membrane.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: GLP1-R has 7 transmembrane helices. These helices form a peptide-binding
      pocket that GLP1 sits in.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: Many transmembrane proteins function as gateways to allow the transport
      of specific substances or signals across the membrane.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: Drugs analogous to GLP1 exist that activate GLP1 R in a more potent way;
      keeping GLP1-R activated longer, ultimately leading to more insulin release.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
